{
 "id": "2023-xie-biophilic",
 "name": "Biophilic Office vs Blue Lighting: Impressions and Ranking",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Xie, Sawyer, Ge & Li (2023), \"Subjective Impression of an Office with Biophilic Design and Blue Lighting: A Pilot Study\", Buildings 13:42 (Carnegie Mellon University, online survey, 284 complete responses). Participants see four renderings of the same private office (Rhino 6 + Enscape 2.7) in random order: (a) baseline with conventional white lighting, (b) blue lighting, (c) indoor plants, (d) daylight and window view. Each office is rated on eight unipolar 7-point scales (lively, calming, comfortable, interesting, spacious, appealing, cheerful, bright), then all four are ranked from 1 to 4 by preference, followed by two optional open questions on what influenced the ratings and preferences. Demographics: gender, age group, years of design education, years of professional architectural experience. Analysis as in the paper: linear mixed-effects model per attribute with the baseline office as reference, plus rank distributions. Stimuli: the paper's own renderings from Figure 1 (CC BY 4.0), credited on the page; the template is removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) the exact scale anchor wording and the wording of the two open questions are not printed in the paper, so the page uses \"1 = not at all … / 7 = very …\" and short paraphrased open questions; (2) images are cropped from the published figure at about 700 px wide instead of the full-resolution renders; (3) the ranking uses one drop-down per office with a check that each rank is used once.",
